SUMMARY:Humber River to Hamilton Beach Niagara Training Ride (55-60km 1 wa
 y)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Bike Meetup\nRiding from Humber Bridge to the end of H
 amilton Beach Trail. This will be a slower ride with a top speed 25 km/hr.
  Fast riders are welcome to ride ahead.\n\nTotal distance should be around
  55-60 km. Road\, gravel or Hybrid bike recommended.\n\nStart Humber Bridg
 e\nRide along Lakeshore (mostly) to Oakville\nStop for breakfast at Aroma 
 or equivalent\n\nContinue along Lakeshore to Burlington & cross the lift b
 ridge\, meet at the washrooms\n\nRide to the end of Hamilton Beach Trail w
 here we officially end.\nOptions to get back:\nGO train from Burlington St
 ation\nRide back\nHave a loved one pick you and your bike up. :)\n\nPossib
 ility of having lunch too depending on timing!\n\n1. You must wear a helme
 t.\n1. make sure your bike is tuned up and carry a spare tube!\n1. Bring $
 $ for the train back.\n1. We are going to have FUN!\n1. If you’ve never 
 done a full Niagara ride\, talk to myself or some of the other riders and 
 we’ll give you tips! Full 160 km (100 mi) Niagara rides to start in June
 /July.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/torontobikemeetup/events/314850662/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260518T190518Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260518T190518Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
